noether 0.1
## Candidate for toffoli_tdepth_spec.ntr: a T-depth-3 Toffoli without ancillas.
##
## Toffoli = H_t · CCZ · H_t, and CCZ|abc⟩ = (−1)^{abc}|abc⟩ = ω^{4abc}|abc⟩ with ω = e^{iπ/4}.
## Over the integers
##     4abc = a + b + c − (a⊕b) − (a⊕c) − (b⊕c) + (a⊕b⊕c),
## so CCZ is seven T / T† phases, each on one wire while that wire holds the parity it needs.
## CNOTs move the wires through (a, b, c) → (a⊕b⊕c, a⊕b, a⊕c) → (a⊕b⊕c, a⊕b, b⊕c) and back.
## The first two layers apply three phases at once, the last applies one: T-depth 3, T-count 7,
## 8 CNOTs.
##
## Expected from `noether eval`: feasible, goal met, fidelity 1,
## tdepth 3, tcount 7, count2q 8 (the textbook circuit has tdepth 4, tcount 7, count2q 6).
def CCZ_{r[3]}:
    T_{r[0]}; T_{r[1]}; T_{r[2]}
    CNOT_{r[0]→r[1]}; CNOT_{r[0]→r[2]}; CNOT_{r[1]→r[0]}; CNOT_{r[2]→r[0]}
    T_{r[0]}; T†_{r[1]}; T†_{r[2]}
    CNOT_{r[1]→r[2]}
    T†_{r[2]}
    CNOT_{r[2]→r[0]}; CNOT_{r[0]→r[1]}; CNOT_{r[1]→r[2]}
def Toffoli3_{r[3]}:
    H_{r[2]}
    CCZ_r
    H_{r[2]}
